      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **[Code Simplicity / Single Source of Truth]** The condition to re-allow deep sleep (`!ccd_ext_is_enabled() \u0026\u0026 gpio_get_level(...) \u0026\u0026 !uartn_is_enabled(...)`) is duplicated across three different functions in `chip/g/rdd.c` and `board/cr50/rdd.c` (conditionally optimized in each place based on what is known).\n\nScattering this invariant makes it brittle if another condition is added later. Please extract a single helper function (e.g., `void rdd_evaluate_sleep_mask(void)` declared in `chip/g/rdd.h`) to enforce this policy centrally:\n\n```c\nvoid rdd_evaluate_sleep_mask(void)\n{\n\tif (ccd_ext_is_enabled() || !gpio_get_level(GPIO_CCD_MODE_L) ||\n\t    uartn_is_enabled(UART_AP)) {\n\t\tdisable_sleep(SLEEP_MASK_RDD);\n\t} else {\n\t\tenable_sleep(SLEEP_MASK_RDD);\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThen, you can simply call `rdd_evaluate_sleep_mask();` immediately after the local state changes in each location (e.g., after `gpio_set_level()` in `rdd_connect()` and `rdd_disconnect()`, after updating `state` in `ccd_ext_detect()`, and after `uartn_enable()` / `uartn_disable()` in `ccd_state_change_hook()`) rather than duplicating the boolean logic and `disable_sleep` / `enable_sleep` calls. [🔗](http://go/tj/aa274f66-4c90-410a-bd54-13e4c58b57af)",
